Infrastructure: Gates

Purpose:
  Defines infrastructure and deployment gates.

InfrastructureGates:
  DockerGate:
    Format: DOCKER-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: Docker build succeeds
    Evidence: build result
    Owner: DevOps

  CICDGate:
    Format: CI-CD-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: CI/CD pipeline passes
    Evidence: pipeline result
    Owner: DevOps

  SecretsGate:
    Format: SECRETS-INFRA-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: No secrets in infrastructure config
    Evidence: scan result
    Owner: Security/DevOps

  NetworkingGate:
    Format: NETWORKING-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: Network config valid
    Evidence: config validation
    Owner: DevOps

  HealthcheckGate:
    Format: HEALTHCHECK-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: Health checks pass
    Evidence: health check result
    Owner: DevOps

  BackupGate:
    Format: BACKUP-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: Backup strategy validated
    Evidence: backup test result
    Owner: DevOps/DBA

  MonitoringGate:
    Format: MONITORING-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: Monitoring configured
    Evidence: monitoring config
    Owner: DevOps

  LoggingGate:
    Format: LOGGING-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: Logging configured
    Evidence: logging config
    Owner: DevOps

DeploymentGates:
  Local:
    Direct deployment
  Staging:
    Rolling deployment
  Production:
    Canary / Blue-Green based on scale

InfrastructureRules:
  [IF1]  Infrastructure gates are environment-specific.
  [IF2]  Production has strictest infrastructure gates.
  [IF3]  Health checks MUST pass before traffic routing.
  [IF4]  Backup and monitoring MUST be verified before production deploy.

State: +
  